15:["$","section","i) There are 2 tasks in writing and both must be completed",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"i) There are 2 tasks in writing and both must be completed"}],[["$","p","ii) For this section will check your use of english language appropriately.",{"children":"ii) For this section will check your use of english language appropriately."}],["$","p","Time for writing format :",{"children":"Time for writing format :"}],["$","p","– 60 mins",{"children":"– 60 mins"}],["$","p","Reading format :-",{"children":"Reading format :-"}],["$","p","i) It consists of 40 questions , made to test your reading skills.",{"children":"i) It consists of 40 questions , made to test your reading skills."}],["$","p","ii) There will be 3 reading passages given to you.",{"children":"ii) There will be 3 reading passages given to you."}],["$","p","Time for reading format :-",{"children":"Time for reading format :-"}],["$","p","60 mins",{"children":"60 mins"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
16:["$","section","Listening format :-",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Listening format :-"}],[["$","p","i) There are 4 parts with 10 questions each .",{"children":"i) There are 4 parts with 10 questions each ."}],["$","p","ii) You will listen to 4 audio recordings of native english speakers.",{"children":"ii) You will listen to 4 audio recordings of native english speakers."}],["$","p","Time for listening section :-",{"children":"Time for listening section :-"}],["$","p","approx 30 mins",{"children":"approx 30 mins"}],["$","p","Speaking format:-",{"children":"Speaking format:-"}],["$","p","i) The speaking test is taken oral between the examiner and the test taker’s.",{"children":"i) The speaking test is taken oral between the examiner and the test taker’s."}],["$","p","ii) There are three parts to the test and each part fulfils a specific function",{"children":"ii) There are three parts to the test and each part fulfils a specific function"}],["$","p","Time for speaking section :-",{"children":"Time for speaking section :-"}],["$","p","11-14 mins",{"children":"11-14 mins"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
17:["$","section","IELTS exam date(2022):-",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"IELTS exam date(2022):-"}],[["$","p","The IELTS test is available multiple times throughout the whole year. Book an IELTS exam date 2022 it is more convenient to them, keeping in mind about your university admission timeline according to that book your slots. Exam takers who are likely to appear for the IELTS are suggested to choose an exam date 3-4 months before their application deadline, to avoid any last-minute rush or error. The IELTS exam is taken across various major cities in India.",{"children":"The IELTS test is available multiple times throughout the whole year. Book an IELTS exam date 2022 it is more convenient to them, keeping in mind about your university admission timeline according to that book your slots. Exam takers who are likely to appear for the IELTS are suggested to choose an exam date 3-4 months before their application deadline, to avoid any last-minute rush or error. The IELTS exam is taken across various major cities in India."}],["$","p","WHAT IS TOEFL?",{"children":"WHAT IS TOEFL?"}],["$","p","The full form of (TOEFL) is Test of English as a Foreign Language. It Is a foreign based english proficiency. This test is taken to check english language ability of non-native speakers .",{"children":"The full form of (TOEFL) is Test of English as a Foreign Language. It Is a foreign based english proficiency. This test is taken to check english language ability of non-native speakers ."}],["$","p","It assesses your ability to both speak and understand English by measuring your English ability through these 4 sections :- reading, speaking, listening and writing.",{"children":"It assesses your ability to both speak and understand English by measuring your English ability through these 4 sections :- reading, speaking, listening and writing."}],["$","p","Types of TOEFL exam?",{"children":"Types of TOEFL exam?"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
18:["$","section","There are 3 types of TOEFL exam :-",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"There are 3 types of TOEFL exam :-"}],[["$","p","This type of test is most preferred mode of the exam and it represents more than 98% of the TOEFL tests given worldwide.",{"children":"This type of test is most preferred mode of the exam and it represents more than 98% of the TOEFL tests given worldwide."}],["$","p","The type of test has been re-launched keeping the pandemic and student safety In mind.",{"children":"The type of test has been re-launched keeping the pandemic and student safety In mind."}],["$","p","3.",{"children":"3."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","TOEFL iBT (Internet-based Test) :-",{"children":"TOEFL iBT (Internet-based Test) :-"}],["$","li","TOEFL Test on Paper :-",{"children":"TOEFL Test on Paper :-"}]]}]]}]
19:["$","section","TOEFL Home Edition :-",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"TOEFL Home Edition :-"}],[["$","p","This type of test is the TOEFL iBT test that is conducted from the safety of the home with a proctor to supervise during the entire time of the TOEFL test.",{"children":"This type of test is the TOEFL iBT test that is conducted from the safety of the home with a proctor to supervise during the entire time of the TOEFL test."}],["$","p","TOEFL exam fees in india:-",{"children":"TOEFL exam fees in india:-"}],["$","p","US $190",{"children":"US $190"}],["$","p","TOEFL EXAM PATTERN",{"children":"TOEFL EXAM PATTERN"}],["$","p","Writing format:-",{"children":"Writing format:-"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
1a:["$","section","ii) Task 1- you will need to read a short passage, listen to short lecture and write accordingly(20mins)",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"ii) Task 1- you will need to read a short passage, listen to short lecture and write accordingly(20mins)"}],[["$","p","iii) Task 2- you will need to write an essay based on personal experience or opinions on given topic.(30mins)",{"children":"iii) Task 2- you will need to write an essay based on personal experience or opinions on given topic.(30mins)"}],["$","p","Reading format:-",{"children":"Reading format:-"}],["$","p","i) Consists of questions based on 3-4 passages.",{"children":"i) Consists of questions based on 3-4 passages."}],["$","p","ii) You have 54-70 mins to answer all the questions in the section.",{"children":"ii) You have 54-70 mins to answer all the questions in the section."}],["$","p","iii) Passages will be mostly based on academic topics.",{"children":"iii) Passages will be mostly based on academic topics."}],["$","p","iv) material that might be found in an UG university textbooks.",{"children":"iv) material that might be found in an UG university textbooks."}],["$","p","Listening format:-",{"children":"Listening format:-"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
1b:["$","section","i) Based on to measure to understand conversations and lectures in english",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"i) Based on to measure to understand conversations and lectures in english"}],[["$","p","ii) You’ll get to hear 3-4 class room based conversations and lectures in english.",{"children":"ii) You’ll get to hear 3-4 class room based conversations and lectures in english."}],["$","p","iii) You can take notes of the audio to help you answer the questions easily.",{"children":"iii) You can take notes of the audio to help you answer the questions easily."}],["$","p","iv) You will have 41-57 minutes to complete this section",{"children":"iv) You will have 41-57 minutes to complete this section"}],["$","p","Speaking format:-",{"children":"Speaking format:-"}],["$","p","i) Based on to measure your ability to speak fluently and effectively .",{"children":"i) Based on to measure your ability to speak fluently and effectively ."}],["$","p","ii) There four questions based on real-life situations you might witness in and outside classroom.",{"children":"ii) There four questions based on real-life situations you might witness in and outside classroom."}],["$","p","iii) Question 1- independent task- requires you to speak completely based on your ideas,opinions and experiences.",{"children":"iii) Question 1- independent task- requires you to speak completely based on your ideas,opinions and experiences."}],["$","p","iv) Question 2-4 – integrated tasks – require you to collab your English-language skills like listening and speaking, or listening, reading and speaking all together.",{"children":"iv) Question 2-4 – integrated tasks – require you to collab your English-language skills like listening and speaking, or listening, reading and speaking all together."}],["$","p","v) You will have 17 mins to complete this section",{"children":"v) You will have 17 mins to complete this section"}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
1c:["$","section","TOEFL Exam date (2022)",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"TOEFL Exam date (2022)"}],[["$","p","The TOEFL exam is held multiple times in a year across different ETS TOEFL test centres. If you are taking the TOEFL exam you should be ready at least a month before your first application deadline. It will give you lot of time to work for your applications, and just in case you need to re-write the exam you can do it after three days of the first attempt. So, if the deadline for your application is october, you should take the TOEFL exam by september. If you feel like retaking the TOEFL, you can take it in the latter half of September again.",{"children":"The TOEFL exam is held multiple times in a year across different ETS TOEFL test centres. If you are taking the TOEFL exam you should be ready at least a month before your first application deadline. It will give you lot of time to work for your applications, and just in case you need to re-write the exam you can do it after three days of the first attempt. So, if the deadline for your application is october, you should take the TOEFL exam by september. If you feel like retaking the TOEFL, you can take it in the latter half of September again."}],["$","p","20 EASY TIPS AND TRICKS TO CRACK (IELTS AND TOEFL)",{"children":"20 EASY TIPS AND TRICKS TO CRACK (IELTS AND TOEFL)"}],["$","p","5 tips for writing section :-",{"children":"5 tips for writing section :-"}],["$","p","vocabulary is a basic of every language. Writing test requires a strong vocabulary . it is not necessary to use heavy or bombastic vocabulary but also, it shouldn’t be more commonly used.",{"children":"vocabulary is a basic of every language. Writing test requires a strong vocabulary . it is not necessary to use heavy or bombastic vocabulary but also, it shouldn’t be more commonly used."}],["$","p","Making grammatical errors could be your major loss. It shows your low knowledge in english language. Focus on using right phrases and tenses while writing. Minor errors are okay but major errors can make your band score drop.",{"children":"Making grammatical errors could be your major loss. It shows your low knowledge in english language. Focus on using right phrases and tenses while writing. Minor errors are okay but major errors can make your band score drop."}],["$","p","Practice writing on your own everyday. Pick a topic- set a timer of 60mins- write- ask your friend or teacher with good english knowledge to analyze it. The more the practice the better the results.",{"children":"Practice writing on your own everyday. Pick a topic- set a timer of 60mins- write- ask your friend or teacher with good english knowledge to analyze it. The more the practice the better the results."}],["$","p","Read as many books as you can, know how to frame sentences. Reading books can be very beneficial to help you with using accurate vocabulary.",{"children":"Read as many books as you can, know how to frame sentences. Reading books can be very beneficial to help you with using accurate vocabulary."}],["$","p","if you are one of them who is a slow writer or doesn’t have a proper time management and end up loosing high score questions.",{"children":"if you are one of them who is a slow writer or doesn’t have a proper time management and end up loosing high score questions."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":["$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28"]}]]}]
1d:["$","section","5 tips for reading section:-",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"5 tips for reading section:-"}],[["$","p","1)Read books,newspapers, articles, magazines:-",{"children":"1)Read books,newspapers, articles, magazines:-"}],["$","p","because most of the reading passages will be given through these sources. It’s important to know the depth of your pronunciations of words . read aloud while you are reading.",{"children":"because most of the reading passages will be given through these sources. It’s important to know the depth of your pronunciations of words . read aloud while you are reading."}],["$","p","2)Watch english news, series and movies :-",{"children":"2)Watch english news, series and movies :-"}],["$","p","watching and listening could help you with your pronunciation and framing of words. Doing this on a regular basis will make you familiar with the accent and pronunciations, giving you a better idea of the native usage of words.",{"children":"watching and listening could help you with your pronunciation and framing of words. Doing this on a regular basis will make you familiar with the accent and pronunciations, giving you a better idea of the native usage of words."}],["$","p","3)Practice pronouncing difficult words and passages:-",{"children":"3)Practice pronouncing difficult words and passages:-"}],["$","p","don’t limit yourself to read basic words or passages. Take note of words which are to pronouncing , listen on google it’s pronounce and make a note of it and practice it.",{"children":"don’t limit yourself to read basic words or passages. Take note of words which are to pronouncing , listen on google it’s pronounce and make a note of it and practice it."}],["$","p","4)Focus on relevant information:-",{"children":"4)Focus on relevant information:-"}],["$","p","it’s not necessary to understand every word or sentence in the passage, Focus on the relevant information and important details to answer the questions.",{"children":"it’s not necessary to understand every word or sentence in the passage, Focus on the relevant information and important details to answer the questions."}],["$","p","5)Skimming & other Reading Techniques :-",{"children":"5)Skimming & other Reading Techniques :-"}],["$","p","learn various reading techniques like skimming, speed reading, scanning etc can help you in building effective reading techniques.",{"children":"learn various reading techniques like skimming, speed reading, scanning etc can help you in building effective reading techniques."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
1e:["$","section","5 tips for listening section",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"5 tips for listening section"}],[["$","p","1)Listen to english podcasts , news, documentary :-",{"children":"1)Listen to english podcasts , news, documentary :-"}],["$","p","build your listening skills by watching and listening to english podcasts,news,etc. This could help you polishing your hearing abilities.",{"children":"build your listening skills by watching and listening to english podcasts,news,etc. This could help you polishing your hearing abilities."}],["$","p","2)Listen to mock audio clips:-",{"children":"2)Listen to mock audio clips:-"}],["$","p","start listening to mock audio clips both in American and british accent. It could help you with understanding the accents and words clearly during the exam.",{"children":"start listening to mock audio clips both in American and british accent. It could help you with understanding the accents and words clearly during the exam."}],["$","p","3)Meditation:-",{"children":"3)Meditation:-"}],["$","p","practice meditation to boost your concentration level. It’s important to stay focused while listening to audio clips.",{"children":"practice meditation to boost your concentration level. It’s important to stay focused while listening to audio clips."}],["$","p","4)Focus on minor details:-",{"children":"4)Focus on minor details:-"}],["$","p","be careful while listening to audio clips , especially during the introduction, because introduction contains all the small and minor but the most important details and information about the situation and characters.",{"children":"be careful while listening to audio clips , especially during the introduction, because introduction contains all the small and minor but the most important details and information about the situation and characters."}],["$","p","5)Pay special attention to keywords:-",{"children":"5)Pay special attention to keywords:-"}],["$","p","as the audio clip will be played only once , pay attention to keywords, as you read the questions, underline the keywords, and try to predict the context of the recordings – who will be speaking, what the speech will be about.",{"children":"as the audio clip will be played only once , pay attention to keywords, as you read the questions, underline the keywords, and try to predict the context of the recordings – who will be speaking, what the speech will be about."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
1f:["$","section","5 tips for speaking section",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"5 tips for speaking section"}],[["$","p","1)Develop a habit to speak in english :-",{"children":"1)Develop a habit to speak in english :-"}],["$","p","start speaking in english . it will help you to speak fluently and improve vocabulary as you speak. If you speak regularly in english with your friends and family it will also improve your fluency and confidence in the language.",{"children":"start speaking in english . it will help you to speak fluently and improve vocabulary as you speak. If you speak regularly in english with your friends and family it will also improve your fluency and confidence in the language."}],["$","p","2)Build your concentration level:-",{"children":"2)Build your concentration level:-"}],["$","p","start building your concentration level by meditating, paying attention to detail, developing listening skills.",{"children":"start building your concentration level by meditating, paying attention to detail, developing listening skills."}],["$","p","3)Involve in the conversation:-",{"children":"3)Involve in the conversation:-"}],["$","p","involve yourself in the conversation. And focus on the questions by keeping your ears wide open.",{"children":"involve yourself in the conversation. And focus on the questions by keeping your ears wide open."}],["$","p","4)Be easy:-",{"children":"4)Be easy:-"}],["$","p","don’t apply too much pressure while speaking, be calm and casual. Speak as if you are a native english speaker.",{"children":"don’t apply too much pressure while speaking, be calm and casual. Speak as if you are a native english speaker."}],["$","p","5)Work on your vocabulary:-",{"children":"5)Work on your vocabulary:-"}],["$","p","work on your vocabulary and grammar thoroughly . it’s important to know what you speak and how you speak. Use correct words and grammar while speaking.",{"children":"work on your vocabulary and grammar thoroughly . it’s important to know what you speak and how you speak. Use correct words and grammar while speaking."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
